 ### [DCX Points-to-Voxels](3783-dcx-points-to-voxels.md)
-DCX Points-to-Voxels converts a point cloud into a sparse voxel grid by mapping points to voxel indices and aggregating features, prioritizing points with higher depth confidence to mitigate noise. It serves as the final aggregation step in the DCX pipeline, contrasting with direct occupancy mapping.
+DCX Points-to-Voxels converts a set of 3D points into a sparse voxel grid representation by mapping each point to a discrete voxel index within a defined bounding box, storing occupancy in a 3D integer array, and computing the centroid of points within each occupied voxel. It differs from simple averaging by prioritizing points with higher depth confidence in its aggregation step, which helps mitigate noise and outliers in regions with uncertain geometry. It serves as the final aggregation step in the DCX pipeline, refining the raw point cloud into a structured sparse representation suitable for downstream rendering or reconstruction tasks. Choose it when depth confidence weighting is required over direct occupancy mapping.
 
 ### [VoxelGrid::CreateFromPointCloudWithinBounds](8505-voxelgrid-createfrompointcloudwithinbounds.md)
-`VoxelGrid::CreateFromPointCloudWithinBounds` voxalizes a point cloud into a sparse voxel grid using a direct hash-map accumulation approach based on a fixed voxel size and minimum bounding box corner, ignoring the maximum bound for coordinate calculation. It is significantly faster than mesh-based voxelization variants.
+`VoxelGrid::CreateFromPointCloudWithinBounds` voxalizes a point cloud into a sparse voxel grid by mapping input points to voxel indices based on a fixed voxel size and a minimum bounding box corner, ignoring the maximum bound for coordinate calculation. It differs from its siblings by using a direct hash-map accumulation approach rather than structured spatial partitioning or multi-plane projections, and is significantly faster than mesh-based voxelization variants. Choose it for high-throughput, direct hash-map accumulation.
 
 ### [Multi-Plane Point Cloud Voxelization and Weight Aggregation](12101-multi-plane-point-cloud-voxelization-and-weight-aggregation.md)
-A pre-processing pipeline that projects a 3D point cloud onto multiple parallel planes based on depth, groups points by 2D grid location and depth bin, and computes aggregation weights for rendering. It reduces outliers and blends points front-to-back using a visibility mask, avoiding z-fighting issues.
+A pre-processing pipeline that projects a 3D point cloud onto multiple parallel planes (voxels) based on depth, groups points by their projected 2D grid location and depth bin, and computes aggregation weights for rendering. It solves the problem of efficiently organizing sparse point cloud data for multi-plane projection rendering by reducing outliers and grouping points spatially. Unlike standard point cloud rasterization which may suffer from z-fighting or require complex sorting, this method aggregates points into discrete depth bins and blends them front-to-back using a visibility mask. Choose it for multi-plane projection rendering.
 
 ### [Point Cloud I/O](15926-point-cloud-i-o.md)
-Reads and writes point cloud data in PLY format, extracting positions, colors, and normals. Supports ASCII and binary layouts with explicit column mapping for CSV/TXT variants.
+Handles the serialization and deserialization of point cloud data, specifically extracting positions, colors, and normals from PLY files for voxelization. It serves as the bridge between raw geometric data and the sparse voxel grid conversion process [Parent](3416-pointcloud-to-sparse-voxel-grid-conversion.md). Unlike [DCX Points-to-Voxels](3783-dcx-points-to-voxels.md) or [VoxelGrid::CreateFromPointCloudWithinBounds](8505-voxelgrid-createfrompointcloudwithinbounds.md) which perform the spatial mapping, this method focuses strictly on file format parsing and writing. Choose it for data ingestion and export.
 
 ### [Point Cloud to Occupancy Grid Conversion with Camera FOV Filtering](22169-point-cloud-to-occupancy-grid-conversion-with-camera-fov-fil.md)
-Converts a LiDAR point cloud into a 3D occupancy grid by filtering points based on the camera's Field of View (FOV) and projecting them into voxel coordinates. It strictly limits input points to those visible within camera intrinsic and extrinsic parameters, ensuring the resulting grid aligns with the visual sensor's perspective.
+This method converts a LiDAR point cloud into a 3D occupancy grid by filtering points based on the camera's Field of View (FOV) and projecting them into voxel coordinates. It differs from general voxelization by strictly limiting the input points to those visible within the camera's intrinsic and extrinsic parameters, ensuring the resulting grid aligns with the visual sensor's perspective. Choose it when sensor-aligned occupancy grids are required.
 
